d the points $(x,y)$ where $∇g(x,y)=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1072 #uuid "a633d445-62c8-5864-b7bf-d694cd1cd56c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y)=(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{y})j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x})j=0\\,i+0\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1=0 \\\\ \\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{{(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81+3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}} & =0 \\\\ 81+3{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-27 \\\\ x & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3,$ we get $y=-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{3}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $∇g(x,y)=0$ at the point: $(-3,-3).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399547 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399548 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399549 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399550 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399551 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399548 131941