ned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399610 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399611 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399612 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399613 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399614 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399613 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1080 #uuid "9d0e5fca-add2-598e-86d3-b4f5c536f2d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1081 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1084 #uuid "7b44e614-ae46-5928-828a-678c7f85761b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1081 "$A$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1084 #uuid "33ac5148-f3ab-50b7-bde0-ea8e82b23438" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1081 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1084 #uuid "b5855a22-7e5b-541c-8834-56bbe6499a25" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1081 "$A$ and $B$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1084 #uuid "1c6ada89-cdaa-544a-8a21-15e02b79999d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1081 "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1084 #uuid "2a6c5c09-c127-5638-b0a9-423f5bc33f89" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399616 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1069 "q-130005" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1071 "Consider the differential equation $x{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+4{x}^{3}y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is a solution to the equation\nII. ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation\nIII. The general solution of the equation is $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1072 #uuid "5007768b-5de4-5206-bbd7-b32aa44bd388" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1074 "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\nx(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=(4{x}^{3}-4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement II is false.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\nx(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2})-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}=(2x-2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}+(4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}=0.\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement II is true.\n\n- So, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution while ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution of the equation, hence $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}$  is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement III is false." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399617 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399618 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399619 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399620 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399621 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399621 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1080 #uuid "f811653b-c37a-5ec9-b2ba-127c51552176" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1084 #uuid "e6f79407-a923-589b-a295-638d183f58c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1084 #uuid "ec6f68ed-dc62-52f7-a8a8-25d2b4e2c679" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1081 "None" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1084 #uuid "304116eb-0764-5f6c