ion of our curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+(-x)^{2} & =2(-x)-2x \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =-4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- For $x=-2,$ we get $y=2,$ and the corresponding point is $(-2,2).$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=0,$ and the corresponding point is $(0,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399624 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399625 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399626 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399627 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399628 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399625 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1080 #uuid "31717cb2-d9d0-54f4-b700-91183260eebd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399624 1081 "$(0,0)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399624 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399624 1084 #uuid "2a3b5cf6-0370-5cde-a9e6-1edabf953fa1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399625 1081 "$(-2,2)$ and $(0,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399625 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399625 1084 #uuid "796d0d95-8bf2-5062-97c0-381c6826adbc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1081 "$(0,2)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1084 #uuid "930c85b6-cd1d-5f01-b245-1181988c9afd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399627 1081 "$(-2,0)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399627 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399627 1084 #uuid "03b48f4a-4c69-5175-9b51-45915a00e587" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399628 1081 "$(-2,0)$ and $(0,2)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399628 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399628 1084 #uuid "36a2c161-410d-5532-af77-2aaed16bed2f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399630 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399629 1069 "q-130256" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399629 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399629 1071 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399629 1072 #uuid "3a8a1c12-7f84-5c3b-83f4-8db057221abd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399629 1074 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is **not** linear. To see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2}) & =a[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+2bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592